{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>and now those born of them</b> — like <b>מהן</b> (from them)." "<b>by the decree of Adonai</b> — to bring near to the congregation of YHWH or to remove, and we have not found that they brought near any of them; and perhaps they removed them because they were not proper converts, the Moabite women. And our Sages, of blessed memory, said: he is our brother for every matter except one born of a maidservant and of a Cuthean woman, and they removed the bondwomen and the children." "<b>and those who tremble at the commandment of our Elohim</b> — so as not to intermarry with them — <b>shall put away their wives</b>." "<b>and according to the Torah it shall be done</b> — to one who does not tremble, for we compel him to put away."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "Resolved ז\"ל as 'of blessed memory' per standard convention for חכמינו."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:26.106927116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}